<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/software>
    a logic:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """The software slice: a five-facet de-conflation of the project domain.

Project ≠ Product ≠ Codebase ≠ Repository ≠ History.

Each facet is separately identified, separately classed, and never bridged by
subclassing or equivalence. DOAP's original sin — collapsing endeavour, product,
repo, and history into one class — is corrected here; DOAP is aligned by reference
as a lossy downcast, never imported (Principle 5).

REUSE.
- Events / Participation / Activity: events.ttl, provenance.ttl
- Contribution / ContributionRole: creative-works.ttl
- VersionSet / VersionMembership: versions.ttl
- Attestation / CryptographicSignature: attestation.ttl, trust.ttl
- contentDigest / versionFingerprint: sources.ttl, versions.ttl
- Temporal / standpoint / displayable: temporal.ttl, standpoint.ttl, core.ttl

The flat property gmeow:developer is REMOVED (Principle 6 — greenfield); the
Contribution relator and hasContributor shortcut supersede it."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/software> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Software Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Software Module — classes, properties, and individuals of the GMEOW super-vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

# exact-one minCount restoration (issue #1194): min-qualified sibling restrictions
# restoring sh:minCount for the reasoner-safe max-qualified exact-one antecedents.
gmeow:Merge logic:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mergeTarget ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects OWL FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.

gmeow:authorIdentityStringFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/software> ;
    rdfs:label "authorIdentityString is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:authorIdentityString is functional: an AuthorIdentity records exactly one raw byte-string — the single 'Name <email>' line as it appeared in the commit object, an immutable historical assertion that is never re-recorded."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:authorIdentityString ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:authorIdentityString ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:authorIdentityString names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:authorIdentityString, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:authorIdentityString and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:authorIdentityString (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:authorIdentityStringFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:authorIdentityString ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
